          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ప్రజాస్వామ్యం — prajāsvāmyaṁ — \"democracy\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ప్రజాస్వామ్యంలో జనమే తమ నాయకులను ఎన్నుకుంటారు. prajāsvāmyaṁlō janamē tama nāyakulanu ennukuṇṭāru. In a democracy the people themselves choose their leaders."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ప్రజా, of the people, + స్వామ్యం, mastery: rule that belongs to the people."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ప్రజాస్వామ్యం (prajāsvāmyaṁ) is built from Sanskrit prajā, \"offspring, people\", and svāmya, \"mastership, ownership, power\" (Monier-Williams); the compound is a modern one."
            }
          ]
        },
